<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<aiml version="1.0">

<!-- Pop phase bank: word-problem recognizers.
     K'UHUL Pop ops: find_best_pattern_match, candidate_sense_bind, gramRead activation.
     Each pattern binds knowns via <think> then fires <srai> to advance to the Sek computation bank. -->

<category>
<pattern>IF * GOING * AND * GOING *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
<think><set name="wtype">rate-distance-time</set></think>
Knowns: object A rate = <star index="2"/>, object B rate = <star index="4"/>.
Rule: rate × time = distance; meeting when distances sum to initial gap.
<srai>WORD PROBLEM RATE DISTANCE <star index="1"/> <star index="2"/> <star index="3"/> <star index="4"/></srai>
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS * PERCENT OF *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
<think><set name="wtype">percentage</set></think>
Percentage problem.
<srai>COMPUTE PERCENT <star/> OF <star index="2"/></srai>
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>SOLVE *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
<think><set name="topic">word-problem</set></think>
Parsing problem: <star/>.
Step 1 — identify question type.
Step 2 — extract knowns and unknowns.
<srai>WORD PROBLEM <star/></srai>
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>SANDBOX DUEL *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
Word-problem sandbox. Both bots active.
KHANARY (Bot A): phase-engine parse + SRILM gram scoring.
NeuralGrammar (Bot B): Qwen3-1.7B generative elaboration.
Submitting: <star/>
<srai>WORD PROBLEM <star/></srai>
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS THE SANDBOX DUEL</pattern>
<template>
sandbox_duel.py runs two bots on the same word problem:
  Bot A — KHANARY.exe uses AIML patterns, SRILM n-gram scoring, and the K'UHUL phase engine.
  Bot B — NeuralGrammar uses Qwen3-1.7B with VerbEngine operation selection.
Both share the word-problem driver (drivers/micronauts/semantic/word-problem.json).
Run: py -3 tools\sandbox_duel.py "your word problem here"
</template>
</category>

</aiml>
